From e5321167d7ed2c12fca0cb01f7e241a4fac15540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:39:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Require the official GBA BIOS again + on-device GBA-detection
 diagnostic log

The bundled open-source BIOS never linked reliably (one lucky v0.4.28 solo
boot; socket 3 fails on retry). Revert to requiring the official 16 KB dump
on both platforms -- the proven-reliable path (v0.4.26) -- and load it for
solo and netplay alike so every client boots the byte-identical image. In
netplay a client without it refuses to boot rather than silently desync; the
launchers block Host/Boot/Join up front on desktop and Android.

Add a self-contained, thread-safe, bounded GBA-detection log (gba_detect.log
in the user GBA dir; path shown on the OSD at boot; Android "Share log"
button). It records, per SI socket, the BIOS loaded and every detection
transition (window-open, auto-reset, quiet enter/exit, link-established,
battle-locked, rematch-release) plus the joybus handshake bytes and a 1/sec
telemetry summary, so a socket-3 stall can be pinpointed (XD-never-handshakes
vs GBA-never-answers). Written transition-only + rate-limited from the CPU
thread through one mutex; never per-poll; not serialized in DoState; no effect
on emulated state or netplay determinism. A withheld (quiet-window) command is
never scored as GBA silence. Works in solo and netplay (each client logs
locally, labeled host/joiner + socket).
